@nsobid-4B159F0F7A360669738390EE8657B4F0
// Astral Chain v1.0.1, applied after Dynamic-FPS 1.0.1.pchtxt and before cutscene-catchup (native_trace --patch,
// in that order). Enabled by AC_FPS_UNLOCKED=1 (setup_game.py); without it this file is not passed at all.
//
// The vendored third_party/AstralChain-Dynamic-FPS/1.0.1.pchtxt is the mod's *Dynamic-60fps* variant v1.1.1.
// Upstream (yogesh1239/AstralChain-Dynamic-FPS, mods/Dynamic-Unlocked/exefs/1.0.1.pchtxt) publishes the same
// v1.1.1 with the rate cap removed. The two variants are byte-identical except for the two words below, which
// both flip a single immediate: `mov w1,#1` (fix the game to 60 FPS) -> `mov w1,#0` (keep its measured target).
// So this is not a second mod: it is the two-word delta, applied as an overlay on the vendored patch.
//
// The timer fixes that make >60 FPS safe are already in the base patch: action/input timers count whole
// 30 FPS ticks instead of frames (so a "15 frame" window means 15/30 s at any refresh rate), the step is
// measured from real frame time, and the camera smooths by frame time. The step floor is 1/16 tick (480 FPS).
// AC_CUTSCENE_FPS=30 still selects the original fixed-step cutscene path at runtime.
//
// Frame pacing is the port's side of this: AC_FPS (launcher "Target FPS", 0 = unthrottled) sets the present
// rate, and the runtime's over-budget check derives its threshold from it instead of the hardcoded 60 Hz one.

@flag offset_shift 0x100

@enabled
009E8D84 01008052 // Init: mov w1,#0 (was #1 in Dynamic-60fps)
009DB6BC 01008052 // Runtime: mov w1,#0 (was #1 in Dynamic-60fps)
@stop
